    {
      "id": "SukqXnnrMbumrwPeYn-po",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 750.798151299505,
      "y": 451.4999613242574,
      "width": 354.63970947265625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526746324,
      "version": 1515,
      "versionNonce": 1084192980,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785998286402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "(The steps are:\n- Upload DNA (FASTQ or BAM files, cancer \nand non-cancer) and optional RNA-seq data\n- Align DNA (-> BAM files) and RNA optionally\n- Get Mutations (-> VCF)\n- Find mutated proteins (throws out \nnon-coding mutations, and checks for \nwhich mutations actually cause amino \nacid changes)\n- HLA Typing (Using Optitype)\n- Initial neoantigen candidate list\n(with sliding window of 8-11 amino acid \nlength sequences around mutations,\nincludes proteins that are partially\nnon-mutated proteins)\n- Protein display prediction (using MHCflurry\nor similar tool) - reranks candidates\n- Predict Immunogenicity (Which neoantigens\nwill T-cells latch on to? Not definitive,\npredict using BigMHC-IM) - reranks again\n- Remove self-peptides by referencing\ndatabases, and optionally removes unread\nproteins based on RNA-seq data\n- Rerank based on: Binding strength \n(agretopicity), expression, clonality, and HLA \nspread. (this menu will include sliders to edit \ninfluence from each of these)\n- Design vaccine sequence and export button\n(using pVACvector, exports FASTA file)\n)",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "(The steps are:\n- Upload DNA (FASTQ or BAM files, cancer \nand non-cancer) and optional RNA-seq data\n- Align DNA (-> BAM files) and RNA optionally\n- Get Mutations (-> VCF)\n- Find mutated proteins (throws out \nnon-coding mutations, and checks for \nwhich mutations actually cause amino \nacid changes)\n- HLA Typing (Using Optitype)\n- Initial neoantigen candidate list\n(with sliding window of 8-11 amino acid \nlength sequences around mutations,\nincludes proteins that are partially\nnon-mutated proteins)\n- Protein display prediction (using MHCflurry\nor similar tool) - reranks candidates\n- Predict Immunogenicity (Which neoantigens\nwill T-cells latch on to? Not definitive,\npredict using BigMHC-IM) - reranks again\n- Remove self-peptides by referencing\ndatabases, and optionally removes unread\nproteins based on RNA-seq data\n- Rerank based on: Binding strength \n(agretopicity), expression, clonality, and HLA \nspread. (this menu will include sliders to edit \ninfluence from each of these)\n- Design vaccine sequence and export button\n(using pVACvector, exports FASTA file)\n)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
